WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.560
While Niwa-kun was hospitalized, I thought,

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.100
he might be a candy-like presence to me.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.800
How should I put it?

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.740
It's a relief to have him close by.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:22.000
It's like craving for a candy when I want something in my mouth.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.500
Maybe he's that kind of presence to me now.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:31.260
Someone I can easily chat with when we're alone.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.970
It gets agonizing when I'm by myself.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:40.520
I can't help but feel that way.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.930
Thanks for waiting.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:51.010
So, is it true that you have a boyfriend now?

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.900
Huh? Ah, wait!

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.370
So that's a yes.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.800
No... boyfriend...

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.950
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.460
Maybe she's talking about Niwa-kun?

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:09.460
I realized that after I spoke, so I wasn't lying.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.090
They say where there's smoke, there's fire.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:17.180
Then, you're saying that fire only erupts in smoky places?

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:21.180
Ryuushi, do you ever think before you talk?

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.890
It's Ryuuko!

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.600
I don't think at all.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.100
Whatever.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.020
Haha, I managed to cover it up.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:33.820
I can never get enough of that look of yours.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.240
Would you like to try my helmet?

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.490
No, no.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.950
It's just that the helmet matches you so well.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.330
I wonder how Granny's doing.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:51.590
What?

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.590
Hello, Granny!

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:01.800
It's the futon girl's filling.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.600
Touwa Erio-san.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.480
Something Ryuushi, or something.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.980
It's Ryuuko.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.620
Let's stop coming here.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:55.630
Huh? Why?

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:58.050
Waif a sheg.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.340
Come on, Erio-chan's here.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.850
Hm. That's true.

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:17.320
Ryuushi, let's go shopping tomorrow.

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:20.440
It's Ryuuko. Tomorrow...

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:24.700
is a Saturday, no clubs,
and the weather's gonna be nice, so...

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:27.410
I already have plans, sorry!

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:38.630
The "plan", as in, ambush at the Tamura shop.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:44.260
When Niwa-kun comes, I'll jump him, with a bang!

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:47.510
But there's a slight problem.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:51.270
It seems there are others on the lookout.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:52.890
Two of them, in fact.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.520
One of them is female,

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.770
hiding on the other side of the street.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.530
Is that the thing they put on cows?

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:04.150
What is he up to?

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:06.160
Trying to get an alien autograph?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:09.030
Could he be an agent for some spacey agency,

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.410
and searching for a tsuchinoko, which turned out to be an alien pet,

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.330
and grabbed in the recent serial animal kidnappings,

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.080
so he's running around the city in search of it?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.300
That was a close call.

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.930
She was the one hiding on the other side of the street.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:29.550
Are you going to the Tamura shop?

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.220
Um... who are you?

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.980
Me? You can call me Smooth-skinned Sensei!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.060
Would you like a drink?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.730
Uh, sure.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:40.480
Are you waiting for someone with bread in your mouth?

00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:42.440
You're a strange one — it's raining out here!

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:47.070
I'm waiting for a friend who's more important to me than the rest!

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:51.660
So, you're struggling with what they call
"more than a friend" in adolescent terms.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:06:01.130
When you put it like that, it fills up this part below my throat.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.630
Hm, hm... that would be love!

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.510
Is that strange?

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.510
It's not a big deal.

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.050
What about you, Smooth-skinned Sensei,

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.550
why are you playing spy?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:11.140
I'm not playing around!

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:14.560
It's more like observing my child at work.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.690
Actually, there's a spy-like man here too.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.060
A man?

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.360
Oh, that's a stalker of aliens.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.280
What an ambitious stalker!

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:26.110
He's a fan of mine.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.910
Does that make you an alien in human skin?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:34.330
The smooth, flattened skin they found in Apollo 11!

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:38.290
Well then, please excuse me!

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:39.750
Have fun!

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.800
Yo!

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.260
You doing well?

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.470
The cous—

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.630
Yo!

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.590
Ryuushi-san?

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.970
H-Hey, Niwa-kun.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.600
It's Ryuuko!

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.600
Hey there, Touwa-san. Morning!

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.560
Morning.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.190
What brings you here today?

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:08.820
What? To buy stuff! I'm shopping!

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.320
Coke?

00:07:13.320 --> 00:07:17.200
This? Smooth-skinned Sensei just gave it to me, just around the corner.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.540
Where have I heard that name before?

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.170
Um...

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.840
W-What?

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.220
Wel...come.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.850
I wish she could've said that when Ryuushi-san first came in.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:39.770
Did you want to buy something?

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.600
Uh, yes! I <i>will</i> buy!

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.020
I'll take this.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:47.440
Thank you... very much!

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:52.780
A-About 120 yen. Please.

00:07:53.820 --> 00:07:54.740
Here.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.250
I guess I'll go see Granny.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:09.800
Is that okay?

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.010
Yeah, but I think she's asleep.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.720
Let me show you the way.

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:26.940
Oh, you're the girl who used to come with a group of friends, but never with Erio.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.020
Uh... yes.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:32.400
I went to a different elementary school.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.410
What? You're not friends?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:44.000
Um... friends... I guess?

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:54.090
Geez, all this clashing denpa, it's terrible.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.590
Don't be flirting in my house!

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.300
Don't go all <i>full color</i> on me!

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:00.640
Take your romantic comedying somewhere else!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:02.480
I'm not "romantic comedying"!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:05.020
Ryuuko-san is in charge of being serious!

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:10.780
Ryuushi-san!

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.690
You forgot this.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.030
Thanks.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:18.200
Huh? Where's the "it's Ryuuko" comeback?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:23.540
Niwa-kun...

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:31.130
I don't really wanna say this, but...

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.250
What?

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:36.510
Touwa-san's reputation is really bad,

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:39.260
especially at our school.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:44.890
So, if you're seen getting along with her, then —

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:46.480
<i>Push!</i>

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:54.650
— might happen. I'm a bit worried about your future.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.160
Isolated and without assistance, huh?

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:03.330
Mikki is... well, she's a friend of mine.

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:07.290
She said we should stop coming here, because Erio-chan is here.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:12.420
I never knew she thought that way.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:16.170
I haven't made up my mind about Touwa-san,

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:19.300
but maybe her reaction was normal.

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:21.300
I guess.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:30.810
Um... listen.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:36.990
Niwa-kun, do you hate me now?

00:10:36.990 --> 00:10:38.950
Are you disappointed in me?

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.990
Why do you ask?

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:46.700
I mean, I'm a bad person.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:52.000
I've been trying my best to show you my good side.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:55.250
So... I mean...

00:10:56.170 --> 00:11:00.680
You wouldn't want to get close to someone dangerous, and you hate to be alone.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.050
Isn't that normal?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:04.310
I-I'm not normal!

00:11:04.310 --> 00:11:08.230
My personality is so unique that it troubles people!

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.480
I'm gonna stab you!

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.100
That's not what I meant...

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.060
I know.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:17.360
I just couldn't stand the serious mood.

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.780
I'm not good with silica-gel things. Yup.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.250
I'll give some thought to what to do about Erio.

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:37.250
You don't need to... but wait, what I said was... I guess that would make...

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:39.630
Ryuushi-san?

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:44.300
I despise my weakness!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.640
I think!

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.310
Erio already left school.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:56.980
But Touwa Erio's influence is still there.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:59.490
It's not fair.

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:09.910
I said I'd think about it, so why am I here?

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:13.670
Not bad. It's better than Erio's tea.

00:12:13.670 --> 00:12:16.540
Why did she wrap herself in your futon?

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:19.710
Who knows? Maybe she's feeling down.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.180
Well?

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:23.840
What?

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:26.600
You're concerned about something.

00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:30.640
People can read minds when they get old?

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:36.150
Anyone could figure that out when you're mumbling, "Why am I...".

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.270
You fool!

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:40.030
May I talk this over with you?

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:41.570
I'll listen,

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:44.780
but I don't give a crap about you.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:57.080
Ryuu<i>ko</i>-san told me that Erio has a reputation for strangeness,

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:59.170
or is actually hated.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.590
Maybe it's because I'm her cousin,

00:13:01.590 --> 00:13:04.380
but I'm somewhat close to Erio.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:08.550
She warned me that I'd be isolated in school if rumor of that spreads.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:09.600
Wait.

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.520
You may continue.

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.190
So I was thinking about what to do.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.520
Hm. I see, I see.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:23.900
Thinking of what to do is just searching for possibilities.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:27.990
You face reality only after you've thought things over.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:31.490
Advice is something you consider afterwards.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:35.120
Like hell I'm going to help you with your fantasy.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:39.130
Clinging to an old hag, you would only drown with me.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:39.960
N-No,

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.710
I was planning from the beginning to think about it on my own.

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:44.010
That's the way.

00:13:44.010 --> 00:13:46.590
Even a fool can come up with something by thinking hard.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:50.550
A fool's thoughts are mostly correct, if you exclude selfish motives.

00:13:51.390 --> 00:13:53.720
Fools are simple-minded, after all.

00:13:56.890 --> 00:14:02.230
My only advice is that you can live without friends.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:07.570
Friends are not oxygen or water.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:10.780
If I had to choose, I'd say they're luxury goods.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.040
It's great to have them,

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.040
but you can survive without.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.620
Not too different from coffee or cigarettes.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.500
That means your friends may become enemies.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:26.590
There's no reason to fear the friends around you.

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:32.720
If isolation scares you, don't live too long.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:34.720
Just look at me.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:39.270
My friends and husband, all dead.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:46.570
Lately, I'm thinking it'll be my turn soon.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:49.860
That's why aliens are starting with their cattle mutilation.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:54.490
Think to your satisfaction.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.580
Think, and be conflicted!

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.840
Can I hang out at your place today, transfer student?

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:11.470
What? Oh, it's not my place.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.850
Oh right, it's Touwa's.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.720
So? Can I?

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.560
M-My parents aren't coming home today...

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:23.810
I thought they didn't live with you.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:24.820
That's true.

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:28.740
Taking a girl home, that's a three-pointer.

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.660
Assuming four-pointers are reserved for special events,

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:34.950
this is a chance for the maximum attainable score in normal life!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:39.410
So I said to myself — but I'm actually just nervous.

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:42.960
O-Oh... you're coming to my home.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.630
Transfer student, you're not picking up any rice.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.420
You keep missing with your chopsticks.

00:15:48.710 --> 00:15:49.970
But why?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.470
Pure interest.

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.570
By the way —

00:15:58.570 --> 00:16:00.850
Do you have any friends?

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.940
The transfer student is my friend.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:05.690
Right.

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:08.820
Another thing.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:11.450
What do you think of Erio?

00:16:11.450 --> 00:16:14.910
There's something that comes to mind when I see her.

00:16:14.910 --> 00:16:15.820
What is it?

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:18.990
If everyone has a place where they fit in,

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:22.160
where exactly would that leave Touwa?

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.090
The place where Erio fits in...

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:30.340
Inside a futon.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:31.550
Bad joke.

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:39.810
Let's go, then.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:45.690
Niwa-kun, where are you guys going?

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.610
We're going to the transfer student's home.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:51.110
Then, we'll do <i>this</i> and <i>that.</i>

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:53.610
What?

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.870
A lot of <i>this</i> and <i>that</i> and even <i>that?</i>

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.410
Don't you think Ryuushi has a surprisingly dirty mind?

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:07.500
Why do you only say things in such misleading ways?

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:11.760
I was assuming we'd play video games and Othello.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.510
You know, <i>this</i> and <i>that.</i>

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:15.010
So you did it on purpose.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:18.260
Maekawa-san is always there to help.

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:27.650
Actually, Ryuuko-san has no club activities today!

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:28.430
'Kay?

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:32.320
I wouldn't mind at all.

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:37.320
I haven't brought girls home since about 6th grade.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:40.450
With both hands full of flowers,

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.950
when I found Erio on the way home, I had to arrange her in the basket.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.830
So this is Touwa's place.

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:53.570
I imagined the wall would be made of futon, but it's a wooden house.

00:17:55.670 --> 00:17:57.180
The door's locked.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:18:00.100
People lock their doors when they're not home.

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:02.470
We usually don't.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:06.280
Everyone inside the house! Did you guys hear that?

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:08.040
It's open.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:12.940
Please.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.700
Coming in!

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:18.030
Coming in.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:22.410
We're home.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:23.930
Welcome!

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:27.480
Oops, that was the greeting for <i>my</i> home.

00:18:29.260 --> 00:18:31.500
What does your family do, Maekawa-san?

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:35.500
Oh, Ryuushi, you live near downtown, so you didn't know.

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:36.990
It's Ryuuko!

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:39.550
We run a bar near the shopping district.

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:42.230
Please visit us when you grow up!

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:46.680
If we stay in business that long, that is.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.830
It's Mr. Pluto!

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.110
How cute!

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.320
That's my...

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:59.860
Tell her yourself.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.080
H-He sits here.

00:19:07.340 --> 00:19:09.310
I'm... sorry?

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:10.600
Geez.

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:16.160
Do you want me to turn into a 179.9 cm tall Mr. Pluto?

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:19.800
That would be a completely different creature.

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:24.550
Then... Then let's head to Niwa-kun's house!

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:28.140
There's nothing interesting
to see there. Seriously.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:30.160
What are you talking about?

00:19:30.160 --> 00:19:34.590
Cards aren't very interesting either.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:38.820
What makes them fun is how you use them.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:42.110
So, this is Niwa-kun's room!

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:46.620
This is where the transfer student lies around all day.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.830
Oh! The cousin's room!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.580
You come here all the time.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:52.460
Can I check out your deep sea fish encyclopedia?

00:19:52.460 --> 00:19:53.420
Sure.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:58.800
What is she looking for?

00:19:58.800 --> 00:20:01.380
I have an idea what.

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:03.970
Not much skin color in this room.

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.430
What kind of impression is that?

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:09.850
What are you doing, the cousin?

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:10.680
Don't roll up.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:14.060
I want to be in relax mode after work.

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:15.900
I'm a hard working 16-year-old.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:17.070
Shut up.

00:20:17.070 --> 00:20:19.070
The futon might smell like me afterward.

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:21.030
That wouldn't make me happy!

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:22.240
Hey, Niwa-kun!

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.410
What is it?

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:25.660
Which one is your favorite?

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:29.330
This one.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:30.250
Helicolenus Hilgendorfi?

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.500
Yes, isn't it beautiful?

00:20:32.500 --> 00:20:34.790
But the background is yucky.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:38.040
The way it stands out is what I like about it.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:42.300
But you shouldn't stand out.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:47.260
Ah! Geez!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:50.600
Hey! Niwa-kun, come here!

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:51.270
Yes?

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:53.230
What else do you like?

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:55.520
Uh, why don't you let the futon go?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:21:00.780
But you see, there's someone determined to be the local mascot.

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:02.820
Maybe you should just let her be.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:05.360
She should just turn into a roll.

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.950
Why is she pouting?

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:07.820
Is she jealous?

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.700
I'll just assume that!

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:15.370
Damn it, experience fails me! I have none!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:17.580
Hey, transfer student!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.290
Look, look.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.010
It's gonna get dusty, and then I'll have to ventilate the room!

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:26.510
That would be a waste!

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:29.640
Why is Maekawa-san sitting there elegantly, smiling?

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:32.060
Go look for porn mags instead!

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:33.180
Niwa-kun!

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:46.070
In the end, I ran over thirty laps between
Erio and Ryuushi-san, futon in hand.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:49.950
I'm home.

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:51.080
Welcome home!

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.540
Mako-kun's friends? Oh, it's you!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.000
Oh, it's the Smooth-skinned Sensei!

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.580
Smooth-skinned Sensei?

00:21:56.580 --> 00:22:01.590
Just as Maekawa-san and Ryuushi-san were leaving, we ran into Meme-san.

00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:05.090
Meme-san whispered something to Maekawa-san.

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.180
Okay! We've decided.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:09.720
I'm going out again.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.600
Oh? Where?

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:13.520
Se-cr-et!

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:15.520
About dinner,

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:17.560
why don't the four of you cook?

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:19.100
C-Cook?

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:21.610
It's the chance to hunt down your dream boyfriend!

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:23.570
Boyfriend?

00:22:23.570 --> 00:22:25.740
I'm the only one here.

00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:28.200
Exactly, you're the only one here.

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:30.870
Yes, indeed....W-What?

00:22:33.410 --> 00:22:37.490
I have to get something from home. I'll be back soon.

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:38.460
Right.

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:40.080
Let's go, Maekawa-chan!

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:41.290
Mom —

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:43.590
bye bye.

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:46.090
Okay, bye.

00:24:27.770 --> 00:24:29.940
Awkward with Ryuushi-san: -2

00:24:29.940 --> 00:24:32.360
Being in conflict about Erio: -2

00:24:32.360 --> 00:24:36.740
Maekawa-san and Ryuushi-san come to Touwa's home. Flowers at my side: +3

00:24:36.740 --> 00:24:39.120
They messed up my room: -2

00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:42.250
30 laps between Ryuushi-san and Erio: -1

00:24:42.250 --> 00:24:44.870
Current adolescence points total: -13

00:24:44.870 --> 00:24:47.960
Next time: The Memorable Day For The Certain Someone.

00:24:47.960 --> 00:24:51.510
It feels as if I've fallen for someone's plan to trap me in a love triangle.

00:24:51.510 --> 00:24:53.470
This unexpected plot development...

00:24:53.470 --> 00:24:55.640
Maekawa-san, hurry back!
